Specifically, firmware/components/st7305/st7305.c is derived from SolarOS's
src/drivers/rlcd_st7305.c. The following are taken from that work:

  * the ST7305 power-on register values and the order they are sent in
    (rlcd_waveshare_settings and rlcd_apply_controller_profile);
  * the CASET address-mirroring rule
        CASET = { mirror_base - addr_end, mirror_base - addr_start }
    with mirror_base = address_start + address_end = 0x3C, which is the one
    piece of knowledge about this panel that is not in any datasheet;
  * the OSCSET/FRCTRL frame-rate pairs for HPM and LPM;
  * the 4x2 pixel-per-byte packing, with the smaller-y pixel in the higher bit.

The framebuffer layout, the landscape coordinate mapping, the damage model,
the gather-on-flush path and the read-back probe are not from SolarOS.

